{
  "id": "T-PEERSEC-1",
  "title": "Peer credential hardening: attested targets only, bound discovery pings, no plaintext credentials off-host, honest local_only wording",
  "goal": "Close three threat-model findings at the root. (A) The cluster peer bearer and any member credential reach only loopback or a peer whose node key is bound in the roster (committed member_add or attested handshake); an unbound Explicit row created from a discovery ping gets no credential and dispatch to it fails naming the missing attestation. (B) Discovery pings are bound to their sender: SUSI_PING_SIG3 MACs the sender's UDP source address and a timestamp; the receiver checks the datagram source, a +-60 s window and a bounded TTL nonce cache, and the unbound legacy tags no longer admit or answer. (C) No credential crosses the network in plaintext: the peer client never sends a bearer to a non-loopback address over http://, and remote plaintext is refused by default on the server for fresh and existing installs. (D) Every user-facing description of local_only says it keeps traffic on this machine and its local network.",
  "size": "L",
